# Per-package coverage floors, enforced by scripts/check-coverage.sh in CI.
#
# A single repo-wide average lets a well-covered package mask an untested one: the
# gate this replaced measured only ./pkg/..., which is 111 lines, and reported 90%
# while the packages holding money, credentials, and the live-mode guardrails went
# unmeasured. Floors are per package and ratchet upward only.
#
# Raise a floor when you raise its coverage. Never lower one to make CI pass.
#
# The money, credential, and safety-gate packages (cli, config, transport, output,
# apperr, redact, permissions, api) are held at the 85% target and marked below.
# internal/update joined them when `lago upgrade` stopped self-installing: it no longer
# downloads a binary, but it is now the code that tells an operator how to upgrade.
# The remaining packages are code generators and doc tooling: a defect there fails
# `make generate-check` visibly rather than moving money, so they carry today's
# measured value as a ratchet floor instead of the 85% bar.

# --- money, credentials, safety gates: 85% target ---------------------------
internal/apperr         94.0
internal/cli            86.0
internal/config         85.0
internal/output         97.0
internal/permissions   100.0
internal/redact        100.0
internal/transport      93.0
internal/update         82.0
pkg/api                 90.0

# --- generators and tooling: ratchet floors ---------------------------------
internal/diagnostics    54.0
internal/docgen         56.0
internal/gen            10.0
internal/generated      50.0
internal/moneycheck     16.0
